# Third-party interfaces

Mod Menu implements two mod-facing APIs that other people defined, so that a mod written
for either one works here without a change. Their authors, and what this project does and
does not take from them:

## ModsSettings API

Renat Iliev (izeberg), https://github.com/izeberg/modssettingsapi

The settings API a mod calls here follows his interface. The Python side of this menu grew
out of Aslain's enhanced edition of that API, which derives from his work. Original credit
and copyright remain with the author. Andrii Andrushchyshyn (poliroid) contributed to that
project and Paul Ekshmidt (Kurzdor) maintained it.

## ModsList API

Andrii Andrushchyshyn (poliroid), MIT, https://gitlab.com/wot-public-mods/mods-list

The window-entry registry here is signature compatible with his, so a mod that registers a
window of its own keeps working. The implementation is this project's own. Where his
package is installed, this menu reads it at runtime and lists what registered with him;
where it is not, this menu answers under that name so those mods still work. No file of
his is contained in this repository or in the released `aslain.modmenu_<version>.wotmod`.

If any code here is ever found to derive from either project, tell me which lines and the
notice for that project will be carried with it, as its licence asks.
